What is the ones digit of 7^35 when written as an integer?To find the ones digit of 7 raised to any positive integer n, we should look at the cycle of ones digits of 7^n, which is 7, 9, 3, 1. This cycle repeats every 4 powers of 7. Therefore, we need to find the remainder, R, when n is divided by 4 to determine the ones digit of 7^n. For example, for n = 35, we have 35 divided by 4 equals 8 with a remainder of 3. Thus, the ones digit of 7^35 is the third digit in the cycle which is 3.
